#. Tag: refentrytitle
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refentrytitle>XtUnmanageChildren</refentrytitle>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refmiscinfo
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Xt - Geometry Management"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refname
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refname>XtUnmanageChildren</refname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refpurpose
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "remove a list of children from a parent widget's managed list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "widgets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "removing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>XtUnmanageChildren</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: date
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "4 March 1996"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: synopsis
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"void XtUnmanageChildren(<replaceable class=\"parameter\">children</"
"replaceable>, <replaceable class=\"parameter\">num_children</replaceable>)\n"
"    WidgetList <replaceable class=\"parameter\">children</replaceable>;\n"
"    Cardinal <replaceable class=\"parameter\">num_children</replaceable>;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inputs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: replaceable
#: index.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "children"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies an array of child widgets. Each child must be of class RectObj or "
"any subclass thereof."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: replaceable
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "num_children"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of elements in <replaceable class=\"parameter"
"\">children</replaceable>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descripcion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<function>XtUnmanageChildren()</function> unmaps the specified widgets and "
"removes them from their parent's geometry management. The widgets will "
"disappear from the screen, and (depending on its parent) may no longer have "
"screen space allocated for them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each of the widgets in the <replaceable class=\"parameter\">children</"
"replaceable> array must have the same parent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See the &ldquo;Algorithm&rdquo; section below for full details of the widget "
"unmanagement procedure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "Usage"
msgstr "Utilizacion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unmanaging widgets is the usual method for temporarily making them "
"invisible. They can be re-managed with <function>XtManageChildren()</"
"function>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can unmap a widget, but leave it under geometry management by calling "
"<function>XtUnmapWidget()</function>. You can destroy a widget's window "
"without destroying the widget by calling <function>XtUnrealizeWidget()</"
"function>. You can destroy a widget completely with <function>XtDestroyWidget"
"()</function>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are only going to unmanage a single widget, it is more convenient to "
"call <function>XtUnmanageChild()</function>. It is often more convenient to "
"call <function>XtUnmanageChild()</function> several times than it is to "
"declare and initialize an array of widgets to pass to "
"<function>XtUnmanageChildren()</function>. Calling "
"<function>XtUnmanageChildren()</function> is more efficient, however, "
"because it only calls the parent's <function>change_managed()</function> "
"method once."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "<function>XtUnmanageChildren()</function> performs the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:334 index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>-</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignores the child if it already is unmanaged or is being destroyed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "Otherwise, if the child is realized, it makes it nonvisible by unmapping it."
msgstr ""

